A||||4||gtsonly||Whats the REAL truth behind Valve Lash???  ORGE????||||5||
Z||000000||gtsonly||12-27-2001||06:45 PM||||I have read through most of the Valve Lash posts and still no real answer to which why to perform this. Most agree the Haynes manual sucks, So what is the real way to do it?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/myfiero001_copy_1.jpg"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Neal||12-27-2001||07:29 PM||||prime your lifters first by setting them in oil and plunging them.<P>tighten the rocker arm till there is no play.  I looke between the valve and rockerarm.  Just lightly lift the rocker at the tip and when you cant lift without plunging the lifter your at zero play, its really easy to eyeball.<P>then tighten 1/2 to 3/4 turn, and your done.||||reg||1
Z||000002||jelly2m8||12-27-2001||09:34 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Neal:<BR><B>prime your lifters first by setting them in oil and plunging them.<P>tighten the rocker arm till there is no play.  I looke between the valve and rockerarm.  Just lightly lift the rocker at the tip and when you cant lift without plunging the lifter your at zero play, its really easy to eyeball.<P>then tighten 1/2 to 3/4 turn, and your done.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P> Yup to Neal, 1/2-3/4 turn.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://users.eastlink.ca/~acook1/pegged%2001.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||wkayl||12-27-2001||09:53 PM||||I did the no play then 1 full turn.  Ran like....well you know.  pulled it apart and backed them off 1/4 turn and now runs great.||||reg||1
Z||000004||GMGW3||12-27-2001||10:43 PM||||I found with some of the higher performance lifters (anti pump up) that even with a good soaking and priming, the initial zero lash and 1/2 turn wont work quite right, it will be enough to get it running, but idle worsens as the lifters pump up. The ONLY way to be sure they are set right is to do a running lash adjustment. While the engine idles, Back each rocker off one at a time till its clicking, tighten it to zero lash and then half a turn. Anti splash clips might help avoid making a mess   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  Old steel rocker covers with the tops cut out also come in handy for this.||||reg||1
